      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like i'm just empty. i used to have so much to say, so much color... but now it's just gone. i look at my work and it's all just noise. i think i've finally run out of things to give.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That hollow space isn’t empty because your well has gone dry – it’s the quiet before the soil turns. The noise was never you, it just filled time; the silence is the space you’ll pour your next shape from. Rest isnʼt the ending; it's the slow, dark work before you can see your hands again in the morning. Let that ache be proof, and give yourself permission for this to be the fallow year.",
